# Jira: Ganesh seva (KAN)

This repository uses the **Ganesh seva** Jira board.

- Site: `https://kesavach.atlassian.net`
- Project key: `KAN`
- Board: https://kesavach.atlassian.net/jira/software/projects/KAN/board
- GitHub: https://github.com/chkesava/expense-tracker-mobile-application-

When creating, searching, updating, or commenting on Jira work:

- Always use project `KAN` unless the user names a different project
- Do not use the sample project `SAM1`
- Prefer `cloudId` `https://kesavach.atlassian.net`
- Keep JQL/CQL page size at 10 unless the user asks for more

## GitHub linking

Put the issue key in the branch name, commit message, and PR title so GitHub for Jira can attach development work to the KAN issue.

- Branch: `KAN-123-short-slug` or `feat/KAN-123-short-slug`
- Commit and PR title must include `KAN-123`
- For Ganesh Seva PRs, put the issue key in the title and a browse link in the body, e.g. https://kesavach.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-123

## Ticket status

Keep the Jira issue in sync with the work. Do not leave status stale.

- When we pick a ticket to implement: move it to **In Progress**, leave a short comment if the plan or scope is not already on the issue, and keep the issue key on the branch/commit/PR.
- While working: comment when the security boundary, UX, or leftovers change.
- When the code is merged to `main` (or the PR is merged): move it to **Done** and comment with the commit/PR link plus leftovers (next tickets).
- Do not mark Done until the merge (or a direct push to `main`) has succeeded.
